---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { publicationPath } from '../lib/site';
const chapters = [
['01','The Bag of Sentences','A pile becomes a claim about what is the same.','chapter-01/'],['02','Piles Are Arguments','Topic gives way to structural comparison.','chapter-02/'],['03','The First Question','The class discovers six recurrent kinds of change.','chapter-03/'],['04','Six Ways Something Can Change','The first six structural families receive their names.','chapter-04/'],['05','Same Change, Different Finish','The same transformation can become sufficient in different ways.','chapter-05/'],['06','Three Ways a Change Becomes Complete','Focal, Distributed, and Release are named.','chapter-06/'],['07','What Is Left When It Is Done?','A third independent structural question appears.','chapter-07/'],['08','Why Does This Keep Showing Up?','The book bends: the children begin wondering why the same structures recur.','chapter-08/'],['09','Three Ways the Result Remains','Standing, Bearing, and Efficacy are named after being discovered.','chapter-09/'],['10','Three Questions, One Thing','The three dimensions locate one completed intelligibility.','chapter-10/'],['11','The Fifty-Four Boxes','The map appears as a compression of distinctions the class has already earned.','chapter-11/'],['12','Move One Dial','The map becomes a field of neighbours.','chapter-12/'],['13','Every Box Can Speak','The Goldmine gives each structural coordinate families of ordinary utterances.','chapter-13/'],['14','The Hard Boxes','Uncertainty becomes something the class can diagnose rather than hide.','chapter-14/'],['15','Sometimes There Is No Box Yet','No completion, no coordinate.','chapter-15/'],['16','Clear Does Not Mean True','Structural intelligibility is separated from truth, evidence and justice.','chapter-16/'],['17','Take It Outside','Prepared examples disappear; the children find and generate structural contrasts for themselves.','chapter-17/'],['18','The Bag Comes Back','The original problem returns. The children know that the first task is deciding what the evidence permits.','chapter-18/']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Pixels of Clarity" description="A complete eighteen-chapter pedagogical introduction to structureacy and the Persistence grammar." sourceStatus="Pedagogical edition · complete · 18 chapters">
<article class="book-home"><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Persistence for Ten-Year-Olds · complete book</p><h1>Pixels of Clarity</h1><p class="lede">A class begins with a bag of ordinary sentences. By sorting, comparing, arguing, testing, and wondering, they gradually discover the structure hidden in things they already understand.</p><div class="progress"><strong>18</strong><span>chapters</span><strong>1</strong><span>unfolding inquiry</span></div><p class="start"><a href={publicationPath('pixels-of-clarity/chapter-01/')}>Start reading →</a></p></header>
<section><p class="eyebrow">The book</p><h2>Read from the beginning</h2><ol class="chapters">{chapters.map(([n,t,note,path])=><li><a href={publicationPath(`pixels-of-clarity/${path}`)}><span class="number">{n}</span><span class="chapter-copy"><strong>{t}</strong><small>{note}</small></span><span class="read">Read →</span></a></li>)}</ol></section>
<section><p class="eyebrow">The final movement</p><h2>The map becomes available rather than compulsory.</h2><p>The book ends where it began: with the old canvas bag and the instruction to arrange what is inside. But the children no longer assume that every item deserves the same kind of judgment. They can locate, compare, ask for context, wait for completion, test truth, and keep questions alive.</p><blockquote>Notice. Do not guess. Go closer.</blockquote></section></article></BaseLayout>
<style>.book-home{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:2rem 0 6rem}.hero{padding:3rem 0 4rem}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(3.5rem,10vw,7.5rem);line-height:.88;letter-spacing:-.06em;margin:.3rem 0 1.4rem}.lede{max-width:47rem;font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2vw,1.5rem);line-height:1.55}.progress{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:.45rem .7rem;margin:1.8rem 0}.progress strong{font:800 2rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif}.progress span{margin-right:1rem;font:700 .75rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;opacity:.65}.start a{font-weight:800;font-size:1.1rem}section{border-top:1px solid var(--border,#d8d3c8);padding:3rem 0}section h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.4rem);letter-spacing:-.04em}.chapters{list-style:none;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--border,#d8d3c8)}.chapters a{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr auto;gap:1rem;align-items:center;padding:1.15rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border,#d8d3c8);color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.chapter-copy{display:grid;gap:.3rem}.chapter-copy small{font-size:.9rem;opacity:.72}.number{font:800 .75rem/1 system-ui,sans-serif;opacity:.5}.read{font-weight:800}blockquote{margin:2rem 0;padding:1rem 1.3rem;border-left:4px solid currentColor;font-size:1.4rem;font-weight:700}@media(max-width:600px){.chapters a{grid-template-columns:2.3rem 1fr}.read{display:none}}</style>
